    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "For adults (18 years and older), the Body Mass Index is given by $B=\\frac{m}{h^2}$ where $m$ is mass in kg and $h$ is height in metres.\n\nFor this question, use the healthy BMI range $21\\le B\\le25$.\n\nWhat is the minimum weight for a 163 cm adult to be considered healthy according to this range? Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$55.79\\text{ kg}$. Use $B=21$ and $h=1.63\\text{ m}$, so $m=21(1.63)^2$.",
      "worked": "$163\\text{ cm}=1.63\\text{ m}$. The minimum BMI in the stated range is $21$.\n$$\\begin{align*}21 &= \\frac{m}{1.63^2}\\\\m &= 21(1.63^2)\\\\m &= 55.7949\\\\m &\\approx 55.79\\text{ kg}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
